WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.030
- And you're Joe.

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:03.123
- Goldberg.

00:00:03.123 --> 00:00:06.290
(romantic jazz music)

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:14.070
Have you been naughty
or nice, little girl?

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.670
When we live together your
place won't be a pigsty.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.703
I'll clean for us.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.570
And you won't eat all this frozen shit,

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.563
I'll cook for you everyday, I promise.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.570
I'll even do your laundry.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.270
- [Woman] No, I can't report him.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.741
That's not how it works.

00:00:34.741 --> 00:00:35.574
- I'm not worried,

00:00:35.574 --> 00:00:36.840
I've seen enough romantic
comedies to know guys

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.660
like me are always
getting in jams like this.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.240
Look at that!

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.570
How dare she invade
your privacy like that!

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.210
It's perverse!

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.950
God, I have to pee.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:51.163
Bec, you've got a stalker.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:55.913
And that was way too much.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:01.040
There it is, with its big naked windows.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.710
It's nice, too nice.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:05.500
I'm thinking subsidized school housing.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.410
Jesus, it's like you've
never seen a horror movie,

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.463
or the news.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:12.523
I'm not bothering you, just checking in.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.259
But then the world
wouldn't know your poetry.

00:01:16.259 --> 00:01:17.909
- How do you know I write poetry?

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.000
- Doesn't every young writer in New York?

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.070
- Should I get the queen
or the king size bed?

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.030
- Your bedroom isn't big
enough to fit a king.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:33.623
- You're right it's too,
how do you know that?

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.110
- It's New York, no one's
bedroom is big enough

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:39.943
to fit a king.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:43.433
- [Man] Hey, let me up.

00:01:44.645 --> 00:01:47.468
- Bec, who the fuck is this?

00:01:47.468 --> 00:01:48.556
(thud)

00:01:48.556 --> 00:01:49.740
(glass breaking)

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.510
But as much I'm hoping
this is just a stage,

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:54.730
that quick password search
on your iPad has revealed

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:56.800
a swipe-fest of millennial manboys.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:58.690
Guy with tiger.

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:00.150
Junior William Morris agent.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:01.050
Viking wannabe.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:02.830
You've been a busy girl, Bec.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.770
It's more competition than I realized.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.070
If I want to win your heart,
I'm going to have to show you.

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:10.763
I'm not a maybe, I'm the one.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:16.130
How do I segueway this
from browsing glassware

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.333
to holy shit, Joe's the one.

00:02:20.826 --> 00:02:22.250
Oh, there it is.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.580
No matter how hard you
fight me, I will always make

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.603
sure you password protect your devices.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:33.050
You are good, Bec, you're medicine.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:36.370
You're the antidote for
liars and you make cheating

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:40.290
a distant memory, right
now I love you so much

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.403
the ringing in my head is music.

00:02:45.613 --> 00:02:47.070
(woman shrieks)

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:52.070
Sometimes we do bad things
for the people we love.

00:03:01.344 --> 00:03:04.011
(woman retches)

